{
  "schema": "headroom.circuit.v1",
  "id": "test-ota-optics",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "OTA and optical devices (validation circuit)",
  "description": "Wave C device bench. A CA3080 VCA (input attenuated 47k/220R into the + input, both inputs referenced through 220R) whose IABC is swept 70-440 uA at 3 Hz through 33k from a moving control voltage, into 10k; an LM13700 OTA-C unity follower (inverting input on its output, 100n to ground) low-passing a divided copy of the VCA output; an incandescent lamp (Uni-Vibe 28 V / 40 mA bulb, thermal state) driven 4-24 V at 4 Hz through 100R, read by two CdS cells (one with the light-history state) as shunts after 47k from the input; an LED/VTL5C3 vactrol driven at 7 Hz shunting the input after 22k; a 2N5457 voltage-controlled resistor with subthreshold smoothing (ksub 70 mV) biased 0.2 V below VTO, shunting the input after 27k. A T4B-style electroluminescent panel behind 4n7, driven 85 V peak at 700 Hz, lights a third node read by an NSL-32 cell shunting the input after 68k.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "work/circuit-netlists/wave-c/DEVICES.md (device research: OTA §1, optical §4, JFET ksub §5.2)"
    },
    {
      "title": "Intersil CA3080 datasheet FN475.5; TI LM13700 datasheet SNOSBW2F"
    }
  ],
